# Budget-64 phase diagnostic launch review

## Verdict

**Bounded diagnostic launch approved, subject to the exact packet bindings below.** The packet is suitable for the one native-only phase run that distinguishes first-pass work from later fixed-point work. It is not an acceptance, adoption, stock-native, performance, or issue-54 closure result. No compiler, runner, hook, backend, or activation was executed for this review.

## Reviewed bindings

The phase candidate is the budget-64 candidate 0c4fd320d50c0ec63c2774fa0b9113c2185b307f0e7402d62922d96ddc45ce03 plus the diagnostic patch d283e5051b34926bac29505bf772589f50ea36a60adf6d856289eb2094fa2825, producing phase compiler 6ce9271c87253070d4d6a9ec60d81d6e2bd6dc7cdfbc49b593a0a52e566eeebe. The launch packet is LAUNCH-REVIEW.json SHA df32fc45e3b5f70efdacd2ae9b7426c2484070d03fd2590c836fbf48f76a96ad. Its native plan is SHA 96c094958ac6997d282a7853898bd24cdd4bcd9e24c3201fa36517cc420a5dea; the outer plan is SHA b5deae527fb08e1c7a274c72197aa9557de24aa43d88d8679f018e061f938e88; and the single-role sequence is SHA 06d11a3655d2a15f1d2e20dfde3d8bb63f5de2e0cf4ce665f100146c4cdbbe0b. The Node syntax-only receipt is bound to syntax SHA 13579bd39a74ff802bc38602133b8f1cd4e670b1a9a7abb8f721c09fc5807917 and reports no compiler execution.

A read-only sweep found all 110 outer pins exact, all five temporary SOURCE02 current/backup pairs exact, the frozen source count 53, archive SHA 404df7dfd9d252d94e44efac0eda017c02e40d0dd65eccd6cdc8415db54192ab, and freeze SHA 4a6f9228b7069f17722f038fca4bea4d5adbee40e833cb9e9ce0d6a344b4f0a8. The earlier research README rebinding is materialized: the outer pin is the current 8bd533cd3fb4775090a573140eb7e835a36c8f258af9bdb0fe0943daf555dbe4.

## Source and marker scope

The patch adds only a local pass counter and diagnostic_phase in compile_book. It emits a short synchronous fd-2 JSON line after was = facts() for pass-begin and after the BRWS ownership update, immediately before the unchanged while (was !== facts()), for pass-end. Each line carries the phase, pass number, fact count, and cumulative process CPU seconds from process.cpuUsage(). Paired begin/end values provide the pass CPU interval; a missing end marker is meaningful on timeout.

The existing fs2 import supplies fs2.writeSync. The patch does not reset or alter OPTIONAL_INLINE_LEFT = 64, emit_open, emit_body, definition traversal, graph closure, or the fixed-point condition. It has no per-definition logging, profile, heap data, intermediate output, generated-source marker, or runtime hook. Its only intended observable is compiler emit stderr, which the unchanged collector retains. Consumer stderr remains required to be empty. The synchronous writes can perturb timing slightly, so marker CPU values are phase diagnostics and cannot support a performance claim.

A pass-begin for pass 1 without a pass-end before the 30-second emit cap establishes that the first pass did not reach the fixed-point boundary. A completed pass 1 followed by pass 2 permits comparison of fact changes and CPU intervals; this is the evidence needed before adapting a repeated-pass skip. An emit timeout or exception may make the existing collector receipt incomplete, but its raw marker stderr and partial artifacts must be retained. That outcome is diagnostic evidence only.

The source and JavaScript cohorts are explicit reuse: source receipt SHA 1321e6e44e142be2e034ab31778f138179c1a91e3c80f0e9a8d2ad6486b8ec34 and JavaScript receipt SHA e2f14afe48769a2deafff01e2d5b623e36ad3c3fd9b90b036575de322a2f46b8, with the complete 207834-byte oracle SHA 14565a3635124edb3ba8ef53b76e2030c3b3698e5d7c4a31989bc3ca9fb54a2d. No new JS execution or universal semantic claim is made.

## Launch and restoration controls

The native plan has one role and invokes the pinned Bun 1.3.14 phase compiler on CPU 3. Its emit, build, and consumer caps are 30, 120, and 5 seconds. It uses the pinned Clang wrapper and resource roots, emits scenario.c, builds scenario.native, and runs the unchanged single-thread, GPU-off consumer against the complete independent oracle. The native plan has 53 source entries and the exact import/resource inventory. It changes no API, core, or runtime source.

The outer sequence takes the distinct component activation lock, checks all 110 pinned inputs, activates only the five frozen SOURCE02 bodies, runs delivery and post-activation boundary preflights, then invokes the single native collector. The activation script verifies the freeze/archive hashes and current backup hashes before writing. Its finally block restores every one of the five backups and verifies their current hashes even if activation, preflight, emit, build, or consumer fails. The collector separately uses the existing heavy lock, so the activation lock and child heavy lock do not alias. Generated C/native paths are absent before launch and are guarded around each command. Raw stdout/stderr, partial timeout capture, guards, and the terminal receipt are retained.

A normal Python exception or handled termination reaches the outer finally restoration. SIGKILL or host loss cannot run finally; the post-run outer receipt and five restored hashes therefore remain mandatory evidence. The outer success assertion expects a complete consumer receipt; if the diagnostic reaches the known emit deadline, it may record INCOMPLETE while still preserving the marker log and restoration result. That must not be reclassified as native acceptance or treated as a reason to discard the phase evidence.

## Remaining gates

After launch, review must verify the exact phase/compiler/plan joins, raw marker stderr, pass-boundary interpretation, complete restoration, and any whole-output result if the emit/build/consumer stages complete. The run does not authorize PR adaptation, adoption of the copied compiler, stock credit, native parity closure, performance credit, or issue-54 closure.